{
	"_comment": "Farms (scripts/sim/farms.gd), for Agriculture companies: farm ports, each with its plots (6 to 12), bought from the land at a price set by the plot's fertility (fertility, from the port and plot ids) and the share of the port's land already taken (plot_price: [poorest with all the land left, richest with the last of it]); a company may own at most max_share of a port's plots, and sell one back to the land for land_sale_share of its price or list it for other Agriculture companies at its own price. A plot grows one crop or is a pasture. A crop's yield a year at full fit is yield_value at its base price (markets.json), times the plot's fertility and its fit (climate_fit between the port's climate and the crop's best climates), shared over its harvest months (crops harvest in their months north of the equator, six months later south of it; at tropical ports a crop not grown all year harvests again six months later), delivered day by day into the company's farm store at the port; an annual crop needs grow_days after planting before it gathers anything and is sown again each year (seed_share of a year's yield at base price), an orchard or vine (orchard) is planted once (sapling_share) and bears fully after orchard_years. Farm workers cost wages_per_plot each pay period for every planted plot or pasture. Weather: a few farm ports a year have a drought or a late frost, drawn for the next year at each new year (shown ahead in the Farms screen): drought_yield of a year's crops (irrigation: irrigated_drought_yield), and a frost takes frost_yield of the fruit, berries and vegetables (not under greenhouses) in its spring; storms over a port take storm_yield of that day's harvest. Pastures: stocked with a breed's herd (head a plot, Better grass more), bought from local breeders at stock_share of its market value at the port; a full herd's young (growth a year, times its fit) go into the store day by day, a herd short of full grows back first. Hard winters (hard_winter_odds a year at cool and continental ports) take hard_winter_loss of a year's young (barns: barn_winter_loss); an outbreak (disease_odds a year, a quarter with vets) takes disease_loss of the herd (half with vets). The store: fresh crops lose their crops' loses_a_day of their value a day (cold store: cold_store_factor of that), dry ones dry_loss_a_day; under spoiled_below they're thrown away. Livestock waits in the pens. Ships of the company's lines that carry it load it free (grain carriers the dry crops, Fresh produce carriers the fresh, livestock carriers the young stock, carrying its breed's value). The Agriculture rating's Farms part (Ratings) is judged from these. Prices are farms' own: farming moves no market price.",
